    <string name="help_dhu_title">Test on a computer (Desktop Head Unit)</string>
    <string name="help_dhu_body">1. In Android Auto settings, tap \"Version and permission info\" 10 times.\n2. In the ⋮ menu, choose \"Start head unit server\".\n3. Connect the phone with USB debugging on. On Samsung, turn off Auto Blocker if it blocks this.\n4. On the computer run:\nadb forward tcp:5277 tcp:5277\n$ANDROID_HOME/extras/google/auto/desktop-head-unit</string>
    <string name="help_car_title">Use it in a real car</string>
    <string name="help_car_body">Android Auto\'s \"Unknown sources\" switch does not apply to apps like this one. Install it through Google Play, for example with Internal App Sharing.</string>
    <string name="help_safety_title">Safety</string>
    <string name="help_safety_body">Don\'t read lyrics while driving. The car screen is for passengers or a parked car.</string>
